# Component Layers

Three layers, one-way dependencies: `src` → `biz-ui` → `design-system` → `utils`. `src` may also import `design-system` and `utils` directly.

- `packages/design-system` (`@landing-page/design-system`): atomic UI with no business meaning (Button, Input, Card).
- `packages/biz-ui` (`@landing-page/biz-ui`): reusable composed UI above atoms, below page logic. Data, routing, and auth come in via props/slots.
- `src/`: routes, tRPC, Zustand, Lingui, NextAuth, and page-only components (`src/app/.../_components`).

## biz-ui may depend on

- `@landing-page/design-system`
- `@landing-page/utils`
- `react` (peer)

## biz-ui must not depend on

- `next` / `next-themes` / `next-auth`
- Lingui, tRPC, Zustand
- `@/`, `~/server`, `mastra-server`
- Vercel Analytics or other app infrastructure

## Extraction

- Put new reusable composed components in `packages/biz-ui` directly.
- Extract from `src` only when a second use appears: drop `@/` imports, convert hooks/store/i18n to props, then switch the import.
- Leave single-route UI in `src/app/.../_components`.
- Do not bulk-migrate existing `src/components`.

Example: a chat bubble shell that only takes `role` and `children` belongs in `biz-ui`. A `ThemeSwitcher` that calls `useTheme()` stays in `src` until it accepts `theme` / `onThemeChange`.
